# FLAT·SIX — core rules

DIY maintenance app for the **Porsche Boxster/Cayman (981 & 987)** — Next.js 14
(App Router) + TypeScript on Vercel + Supabase, with an MCP server for Claude.
Full rules in [`CLAUDE.md`](mdc:CLAUDE.md); runbooks in
[`docs/procedures/`](mdc:docs/procedures).

## Golden rule

A change isn't done until the **five layers** it touches are consistent:
**Data** (`lib/`) · **Backend** (`supabase/migrations/` + `lib/db/*`) · **UI**
(`app/` + `components/`) · **MCP** (`lib/mcp/tools.ts`) · **Docs**
(`docs/procedures/` + `CLAUDE.md` + `.cursor/rules/`).

## Key facts

- Static reference data lives in `lib/` (`data.ts`, `models.ts`, `knowledge/`,
  `fitment/`, `documents.ts`, `credits.ts`). `lib/models.ts` (`CAR_VARIANTS`) is the
  single source of truth for models.
- Per-user data is in Postgres via `lib/db/*`; RLS = `auth.uid() = user_id`.
- Knowledge/specs are **per generation** — never let 981 and 987 data cross.
- Backend change → additive Supabase migration + `lib/db/*` mapping + `lib/types.ts`.
- **A new user-facing capability the AI should use → add an MCP tool**
  (`lib/mcp/tools.ts`); knowledge/computation tools no-auth, garage tools
  token-scoped, always generation-scoped. Validate before shipping.
- Data claims (specs/torque/alignment) must be sourced or flagged `unconfirmed`.
- Manual search (`manual_sections`) is hybrid FTS + Voyage/pgvector embeddings.
  After importing doc text, run `npm run db:embed-manual` (needs `VOYAGE_API_KEY`)
  so semantic search sees it. Torque finder is FTS-only, no embeddings.

## Before non-trivial work

Read the matching runbook: adding-documents / adding-model-variant /
adding-new-generation / building-features. **When you change a process, update its
procedure doc + `CLAUDE.md` + these rules.**

## Verify

Lint isn't configured — **`npx tsc --noEmit` is the gate.** Unit-check pure logic;
run the app and drive the real flow (mobile at 375 px too).
